/T (Bucket aggregations: Documents can be grouped into buckets by using bucket aggregations. You can use them to create data buckets or group data. A bucket can be formed based on existing field values, ranges, etc. Metric aggregations: This aggregation helps to calculate metrics \(such as a sum, or average\) based on field values. Pipeline aggregations: This type of aggregation takes inputs from the output results of other aggregates rather than individual documents or fields.)
